#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SPANK plugin for QRMI {#spank-plugin-for-qrmi}"
msgstr "Plugin SPANK untuk QRMI {#spank-plugin-for-qrmi}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) for "
"the [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) is used to "
"configure access to quantum resources from user jobs in a compute "
"environment administrated by the "
"[Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html) workload manager. It "
"handles the acquisition and release of access to quantum resources and sets "
"the necessary environment variables for executing quantum workloads. The "
"available quantum resources are specified in a `qrmi_config.json` file, "
"which is managed by an administrator.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Plugin SPANK](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) untuk "
"[Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) digunakan untuk"
" mengkonfigurasi akses kepada sumber kuantum daripada kerja pengguna dalam "
"persekitaran pengkomputeran yang ditadbir oleh pengurus beban kerja "
"[Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html). Ia mengendalikan "
"pemerolehan dan pelepasan akses kepada sumber kuantum serta menetapkan "
"pemboleh ubah persekitaran yang diperlukan untuk melaksanakan beban kerja "
"kuantum. Sumber kuantum yang tersedia ditentukan dalam fail "
"`qrmi_config.json`, yang diurus oleh pentadbir.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once installed, this plugin registers the following option. A Slurm user can"
" specify which quantum resources are used for the Slurm job script.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah dipasang, plugin ini mendaftarkan opsyen berikut. Pengguna Slurm "
"boleh menentukan sumber kuantum yang digunakan untuk skrip kerja Slurm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For example,\n"
msgstr "Contohnya,\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements and configuration {#requirements-and-configuration}"
msgstr "Keperluan dan konfigurasi {#requirements-and-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following tools are required for the compiling environment:\n"
"* [Rust compiler](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) 1.86 or above\n"
"* A C compiler: for example, GCC (gcc) on Linux and Clang (clang-tools-extra) for Rust unknown targets/cross compilations. QRMI and its SPANK plugin are compatible with a compiler conforming to the C11 standard\n"
"* make/cmake (make/cmake RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
"* openssl (openssl-devel RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
"* zlib (zlib-devel RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
"* Slurm header files(slurm/slurm.h and so forth) must be available on your host\n"
msgstr ""
"Alat berikut diperlukan untuk persekitaran pengkompilan:\n"
"* [Pengkompil Rust](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) 1.86 atau ke atas\n"
"* Pengkompil C: contohnya, GCC (gcc) pada Linux dan Clang (clang-tools-extra) untuk sasaran Rust yang tidak diketahui/pengkompilan silang. QRMI dan plugin SPANK-nya serasi dengan pengkompil yang mematuhi standard C11\n"
"* make/cmake (make/cmake RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"
"* openssl (openssl-devel RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"
"* zlib (zlib-devel RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"
"* Fail pengepala Slurm (slurm/slurm.h dan sebagainya) mesti tersedia pada hos anda\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The runtime environment requires:\n"
"* gcc (libgcc RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
"* openssl (openssl-libs RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
"* zlib (zlib RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr ""
"Persekitaran masa jalan memerlukan:\n"
"* gcc (libgcc RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"
"* openssl (openssl-libs RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"
"* zlib (zlib RPM untuk OS serasi RHEL)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Configure available quantum resources {#configure-available-quantum-"
"resources}"
msgstr ""
"Konfigurasi sumber kuantum yang tersedia {#configure-available-quantum-"
"resources}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The repository contains an example configuration "
"([`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-"
"plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Repositori mengandungi contoh konfigurasi "
"([`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-"
"plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `resources` array contains a set of available quantum resources. Each "
"quantum resource definition contains the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Array `resources` mengandungi set sumber kuantum yang tersedia. Setiap "
"definisi sumber kuantum mengandungi yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Property | Description |\n"
"| ---- | ---- |\n"
"| name | Quantum resource name (for example, backend name) |\n"
"| type | Resource type (`direct-access`, `qiskit-runtime-service` and `pasqal-cloud`) |\n"
"| environment | A set of environment variables to work with QRMI. Current implementations assume API endpoint and credentials are specified via environment variable setting |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sifat | Penerangan |\n"
"| ---- | ---- |\n"
"| name | Nama sumber kuantum (contohnya, nama Backend) |\n"
"| type | Jenis sumber (`direct-access`, `qiskit-runtime-service` dan `pasqal-cloud`) |\n"
"| environment | Set pemboleh ubah persekitaran untuk bekerja dengan QRMI. Pelaksanaan semasa menganggap titik akhir API dan kelayakan ditentukan melalui tetapan pemboleh ubah persekitaran |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a user specifies a resource with the `--qpu` option that is not defined "
"in the `qrmi_config.json` file, the specification will be ignored.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika pengguna menentukan sumber dengan opsyen `--qpu` yang tidak ditakrifkan"
" dalam fail `qrmi_config.json`, spesifikasi itu akan diabaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the user sets the necessary environment variables for job execution "
"themselves, it is not required to specify them in this file. In this case, "
"the environment property will be `{}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika pengguna menetapkan pemboleh ubah persekitaran yang diperlukan untuk "
"pelaksanaan kerja sendiri, tidak perlu menentukannya dalam fail ini. Dalam "
"kes ini, sifat persekitaran akan menjadi `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you are using a QPU resource with the resource type `qiskit-runtime-service`, use an account that supports [opening a session](/guides/run-jobs-session#open-a-session), such as a Premium Plan account.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Jika anda menggunakan sumber QPU dengan jenis sumber `qiskit-runtime-service`, gunakan akaun yang menyokong [membuka sesi](/guides/run-jobs-session#open-a-session), seperti akaun Premium Plan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using an account that does not support opening a session, such as an Open Plan account, add `QRMI_IBM_QRS_SESSION_MODE=\"batch\"` to the environment variable list in qrmi_config.json as aworkaround.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda menggunakan akaun yang tidak menyokong pembukaan sesi, seperti akaun Open Plan, tambahkan `QRMI_IBM_QRS_SESSION_MODE=\"batch\"` ke senarai pemboleh ubah persekitaran dalam qrmi_config.json sebagai penyelesaian sementara.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Installation {#installation}"
msgstr "Pemasangan {#installation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the build using `make` and `cmake`:\n"
msgstr "Jalankan binaan menggunakan `make` dan `cmake`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the `CMakeLists.txt` file expects the Slurm header file "
"(`slurm.h`) to be located in `/usr/include/slurm`, but this can be "
"customized as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lalai, fail `CMakeLists.txt` menjangkakan fail pengepala Slurm "
"(`slurm.h`) berada di `/usr/include/slurm`, tetapi ini boleh disesuaikan "
"seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the above build step is successful, a Linux shared library named "
"`spank_qrmi.so` will be created under the `build/` directory. \n"
msgstr ""
"Jika langkah binaan di atas berjaya, pustaka kongsi Linux bernama "
"`spank_qrmi.so` akan dicipta di bawah direktori `build/`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition, add the following one line to the `/etc/slurm/plugstack.conf` "
"on the nodes where this plugin is installed (note that an administrator "
"needs to create the `qrmi_config.json` file and specify the path as a plugin"
" argument, as in the following):\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, tambahkan satu baris berikut ke `/etc/slurm/plugstack.conf` pada"
" nod di mana plugin ini dipasang (perhatikan bahawa pentadbir perlu mencipta"
" fail `qrmi_config.json` dan menentukan laluan sebagai argumen plugin, "
"seperti berikut):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use the available optional arguments to add environment variables to"
" the Slurm process where the SPANK plugin is loaded. The format for "
"specifying environment variables is defined as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh menggunakan argumen opsional yang tersedia untuk menambah "
"pemboleh ubah persekitaran kepada proses Slurm di mana plugin SPANK "
"dimuatkan. Format untuk menentukan pemboleh ubah persekitaran ditakrifkan "
"seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, when interacting with quantum resources via an HTTP proxy, the "
"environment variables `http_proxy`, `https_proxy`, and `no_proxy` are "
"required. These can be added as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contohnya, apabila berinteraksi dengan sumber kuantum melalui proksi HTTP, "
"pemboleh ubah persekitaran `http_proxy`, `https_proxy`, dan `no_proxy` "
"diperlukan. Ini boleh ditambahkan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the allocator node, your don't need to specify the path to "
"qrmi_config.json, as in the following.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk nod pengagih, anda tidak perlu menentukan laluan ke qrmi_config.json, "
"seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following table shows which Slurm context nodes these files should be copied to. For more details of each context, refer to the [documentation](https://slurm.schedmd.com/spank.html#SECTION_SPANK-PLUGINS) for the SPANK plugin.\n"
"| Files | Slurm contexts |\n"
"| ------- | ------- |\n"
"| `plugstack.conf` | **local**, **remote**, **allocator**, **slurmd**, and **job_script** |\n"
"| `qrmi_config.json` | **remote** (Compute nodes) |\n"
"| `spank_qrmi.so` | **allocator** and **remote** (Login nodes and compute nodes) |\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadual berikut menunjukkan nod konteks Slurm yang fail ini perlu disalin ke dalamnya. Untuk butiran lanjut setiap konteks, rujuk [dokumentasi](https://slurm.schedmd.com/spank.html#SECTION_SPANK-PLUGINS) untuk plugin SPANK.\n"
"| Fail | Konteks Slurm |\n"
"| ------- | ------- |\n"
"| `plugstack.conf` | **local**, **remote**, **allocator**, **slurmd**, dan **job_script** |\n"
"| `qrmi_config.json` | **remote** (Nod pengiraan) |\n"
"| `spank_qrmi.so` | **allocator** dan **remote** (Nod log masuk dan nod pengiraan) |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Once `plugstack.conf` is updated, SPANK plugins will be loaded at runtime during the next job launch, which means administrators do not need to restart the Slurm cluster.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Setelah `plugstack.conf` dikemas kini, plugin SPANK akan dimuatkan pada masa jalan semasa pelancaran kerja seterusnya, bermakna pentadbir tidak perlu memulakan semula kluster Slurm.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once you complete installation, you should find the `--qpu=names` option in "
"the `sbatch` help message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah selesai pemasangan, anda akan menemui opsyen `--qpu=names` dalam "
"mesej bantuan `sbatch`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging {#logging}"
msgstr "Pengelogan {#logging}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This plugin uses the Slurm logger for logging. Log messages from this plugin"
" can be found in `/var/log/slurm/slurmd.log`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plugin ini menggunakan pencatat Slurm untuk pengelogan. Mesej log daripada "
"plugin ini boleh ditemui di `/var/log/slurm/slurmd.log`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable the QRMI runtime log by specifying the following `srun` "
"arguments.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan log masa jalan QRMI dengan menentukan argumen `srun` "
"berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|  `sbatch`/`srun` option | Slurm log level (SRUN_DEBUG) | QRMI log level (RUST_LOG) |\n"
"| ---- | ---- | ---- |\n"
"| (default) | 3 | info |\n"
"| `--quiet` | 2 | error |\n"
"| `--verbose` | 4 | debug |\n"
"| `-vv` or more | 5 | trace |\n"
msgstr ""
"|  Opsyen `sbatch`/`srun` | Tahap log Slurm (SRUN_DEBUG) | Tahap log QRMI (RUST_LOG) |\n"
"| ---- | ---- | ---- |\n"
"| (lalai) | 3 | info |\n"
"| `--quiet` | 2 | error |\n"
"| `--verbose` | 4 | debug |\n"
"| `-vv` atau lebih | 5 | trace |\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for multiple QPUs {#considerations-for-multiple-qpus}"
msgstr "Pertimbangan untuk pelbagai QPU {#considerations-for-multiple-qpus}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At runtime, each QRMI instance is linked to a single QPU resource. To enable"
" the use of multiple quantum resources within a single job script, this "
"plugin sets environment variables with the resource name as a prefix. For "
"example, if `--qpu=qpu1,qpu2` is specified, the environment variables will "
"be set as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada masa jalan, setiap contoh QRMI dikaitkan dengan satu sumber QPU. Untuk "
"membolehkan penggunaan beberapa sumber kuantum dalam satu skrip kerja, "
"plugin ini menetapkan pemboleh ubah persekitaran dengan nama sumber sebagai "
"awalan. Contohnya, jika `--qpu=qpu1,qpu2` ditentukan, pemboleh ubah "
"persekitaran akan ditetapkan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This ensures that each QRMI instance operates with the configuration "
"parameters set for its respective resource during the execution of the Slurm"
" job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini memastikan setiap contoh QRMI beroperasi dengan parameter konfigurasi "
"yang ditetapkan untuk sumbernya masing-masing semasa pelaksanaan kerja "
"Slurm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The above environment variable settings are applied only to jobs where the "
"`--qpu=names` option is specified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tetapan pemboleh ubah persekitaran di atas hanya digunakan untuk kerja di "
"mana opsyen `--qpu=names` ditentukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This plugin also sets the following two environment variables, which are "
"referred by the QRMI primitives code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plugin ini juga menetapkan dua pemboleh ubah persekitaran berikut, yang "
"dirujuk oleh kod primitif QRMI.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Environment variable | Description |\n"
"| ---- | ---- |\n"
"| `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` | Comma-separated list of QPU resources to use at runtime. Undocumented resources will be filtered out. For example, `qpu1,qpu2` |\n"
"| `SLURM_JOB_QPU_TYPES` | Comma-separated list of resource type (`direct-access`, `qiskit-runtime-service`, and `pasqal-cloud`). For example, `direct-access,pasqal-cloud` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Pemboleh ubah persekitaran | Penerangan |\n"
"| ---- | ---- |\n"
"| `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` | Senarai dipisahkan koma sumber QPU yang digunakan pada masa jalan. Sumber yang tidak didokumentasikan akan ditapis keluar. Contohnya, `qpu1,qpu2` |\n"
"| `SLURM_JOB_QPU_TYPES` | Senarai dipisahkan koma jenis sumber (`direct-access`, `qiskit-runtime-service`, dan `pasqal-cloud`). Contohnya, `direct-access,pasqal-cloud` |\n"
